{"@context":{"skos":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#","dcterms":"http://purl.org/dc/terms/","@language":{"@container":"@language"}},"@id":"https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0136","@type":"skos:Concept","skos:notation":"dpp-0136","skos:prefLabel":{"eng":"blind edge"},"skos:definition":{"eng":"edge on a typed passport relationship whose existence and endpoints are concealed from all observers, so that a child-to-parent reference does not reveal where a thing is — a household or a site"},"skos:scopeNote":{"eng":"Edge visibility classes — public, restricted (role-qualified), blind and escrowed — are declared on every relationship; the installation schema (concept dpp-0142) carries visibility as an edge class with escrow arrangement (concept dpp-0137) and audiences."}}